course: dictionary
lesson: 13426
title: A word from another language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come into English from other languages. Hombre is one of them. In Spanish, hombre means man. In US slang, and in cowboy films, people also use it to mean a man or a guy. «That hombre looks tough.» The cowboy setting and the word tough are your clues, so the speaker means a tough man.
explain: Hombre is not really an English word, so you will not find it in every English book. Look at the words around it. «The sheriff warned the bad hombre to leave town.» The word bad tells you this man causes trouble, and the sheriff tells you the story is about law and order in a town.
explain: When you are still not sure, check a dictionary. A dictionary can tell you where a word comes from and whether it is slang. Slang is informal language that people use in everyday talk, not in formal writing.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Hombre» means man in Spanish.
fact: In US slang, «hombre» means a man or a guy.
fact: «Tough hombre» means a strong, hard man, the kind who is not easily beaten.
fact: A word taken from another language and used in English is called a loanword.
exercise: «The hombre rode into town on a grey horse.» What does hombre mean here? | *A man | A horse | A town
exercise: In Spanish, hombre means which of these? | *Man | Sun | Town | Horse
exercise: «He was a tough hombre, and nobody argued with him.» What does tough hombre mean? | A hungry dog | A kind teacher | A small, gentle child | *A strong, hard man
test: Hombre is a word from which language? | *Spanish | French | German
test: «The bad hombre took the money and ran.» What does bad hombre most likely mean? | *A man who causes trouble | A man who cooks well | A good friend
exam: A child reads «a tough hombre» and does not know hombre. What should they do first? | Skip every word that is hard to say | Guess that it means a horse | *Read the words around it and look for clues | Stop reading the book forever
